    The SSC, DRDO and Army figures come from published summaries of the notices, so check the official
    notice for the final numbers.
  </p>

  <p>
    A practical point on timing: ESE prelims on 31 January 2027 fall just before the GATE window
    that begins on 6 February 2027. Civil, mechanical, electrical and electronics engineers share a lot
    of core-subject preparation across the two, which is why many aspirants prepare for both together.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      <strong>Two filters, not one.</strong> A good GATE score opens the door. Each PSU or department
      then runs its own separate selection with limited seats, often with an interview or group
      discussion. A strong score with no offer is a common outcome. Run a skill or income route in
      parallel, and set a checkpoint date with your family rather than an open-ended attempt count.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Pay in this lane follows fixed bands. SSC JE, for example, lists Level 6 pay of Rs 35,400 to
    Rs 1,12,400 in the notice, plus allowances. Stability, leave and benefits are real advantages. The
    trade-off is limited scalable income: outside-work rules vary by service, so verify them for the
    specific post. If this lane is your main plan, the
    <a href="/blog/government-jobs/psu-jobs-after-engineering-india/">PSU jobs after engineering</a> and
    <a href="/blog/government-jobs/government-jobs-after-engineering-india/">government jobs after engineering</a>
    guides compare the pay ladders in detail.
  </p>

